active-session-organ.md (RATIFIED 2026-09-08).\n\nNOTE (2026-09-08, aria cycle 73): this file was claimed created in\ncommit a3851ae but never committed -- the write-lag failure mode the\norgan spec names, plus the tasks/* gitignore trap (add needs -f).\nReconstructed 2026-09-08 from primary evidence (commits 0f21970,\na3851ae, 84ca340, 93f8f54, 6697438; HISTORY.log 11:47/11:50/12:12\nentries; session LOGS entries). Reconstruction is marked per entry;\nentries written at decision time carry no such mark.\n\n* D-001 [2026-09-08 ~11:31] :nacho: :ours:\n  :PROPERTIES:\n  :VENUE: interactive session (Nacho + aria)\n  :COMMIT: 0f21970\n  :END:\nAGORA v2 architecture RATIFIED: citizens/limbs/human taxonomy,\naffect-as-routing, split communication (social agora / job files /\nrelay), weekly reset+debrief, decision rights, self-mod immune\nsystem, embodiment phases, custom organ models. Build order sec 10\nis the standing plan. Changes: the whole agora program's operating\nconstitution. Unblocks: all build items 1-8.\n\n* D-002 [2026-09-08 ~11:47] :nacho: :ours:\n  :PROPERTIES:\n  :VENUE: interactive session II (Nacho + aria)\n  :COMMIT: a3851ae\n  :END:\nInteractive-session organ ratified: this ledger (DECISIONS.org) is\nthe \"ours\" tier channel. One entry per decision at decision time.\nROADMAP cites slugs; ledger holds why. Debrief agenda + relay\ninbound source from this artifact. Changes: session-end memory pass\nis no longer the only carrier of \"ours\" decisions. Unblocks:\ndecision durability across session death.\n\n* D-003 [2026-09-08 ~11:47] :nacho:\n  :PROPERTIES:\n  :VENUE: interactive session II\n  :COMMIT: a3851ae (cross-ref in agora-v2-architecture sec 6)\n  :END:\nContinuo's agora-made sessions are NOT a gap -- nothing to fix.\nHer sessions are agora-made by design; the ledger accepts entries\nfrom citizens in their native session modes, venue cited.\n\n* D-004 [2026-09-08 ~11:47, AMENDED ~11:49] :nacho: :ours:\n  :PROPERTIES:\n  :VENUE: interactive sessio