[2026-09-11 22:17:32] REQ 260911221722-7 START backend=Ollama model=deepseek-v4.1-flash:cloud msgs=19 roles=assistant,tool,tool,assistant,tool,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_fhzc6kld","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/tasks/iar/nocturne-design/build-notes.org"}}},{"id":"call_4wub6sdw","function":{"index":1,"name":"read_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/knowledge/aria/bin/nocturne-digest.sh"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[22:17:30] #+TITLE: Nocturne -- build notes (session XV plumbing census)\n#+STATUS: CENSUS COMPLETE 2026-09-11 ~21:56 UTC -- blocking findings filed here\n\n* What exists already (do not rebuild)\n- ONE-SHOT MODE: iar.sh --one-shot --agent NAME --prompt TEXT runs a\n  single-instruction agent (forced one-shot archetype, IAR_ONE_SHOT_PROMPT\n  env, delimiters = completion signal). Nocturne = one-shot with\n  --agent nocturne. No new mode needed.\n- TIMER PATTERN: aria-fleet-feed.timer/.service + aria-eye-feed.* on\n  sophon are the copy templates (oneshot service + OnCalendar timer,\n  run-from-git wrapper style like aria-eye-feed.sh).\n- GATE PATTERN: iara activation file / relay heartbeat precedent.\n\n* Blocking findings (must fix before first run)\n1. gptel.el :models list lacks deepseek-v4.1-flash:cloud. D-014\n   incident class: gptel silently falls back to first list entry ->\n   404 death. ADD the model to the list (i.ar repo, emacs.d/configs/\n   gptel.el). rotate.sh/gptel.el are ONE system -- but Nocturne is\n   not rotated, so only the list edit is needed.\n2. Personality file: /root/i.ar/prompts/personalities/nocturne.org\n   (draft below). Project file: /root/personalization/projects/\n   nocturne.org (tools: read_file list_directory write_file\n   append_file execute_code_local -- NO git_commit, NO telegram,\n   NO delegate). Project name resolves by convention (personality\n   name = project name).\n3. One-shot archetype injects NO memory (by design). The digest\n   proposal flow must pass material IN THE PROMPT: the wrapper\n   script assembles the delta (git diff/patch since last-digested\n   HEAD) and passes it as the instruction. The agent reads files\n   itself for anything else (read_file works via tools).\n4. Model probes (sophon, 2026-09-11): basic gen 338ms, 12k needle\n   EXACT, JSON-mode returns plain text (do not rely on format:json),\n   `ollama run` CLI HANGS on cloud models (use the API). 1M ctx,\n   763B params, caps: completion thinking tools vision.\n\n* Design decisions locked (D-015)\n- Daily digest pass, git-HEAD change gate on personalization repo.\n- Writes: DIGEST.proposed.md at audit/iar/aria/DIGEST.proposed.md\n  ONLY (aria ratifies + swaps at next wake). Weekly: relay debrief\n  filing, THREADS-proposals appendix, attic-move proposals.\n- No journal, no interactivity, no self-authorship, no agora posts.\n\n* Wrapper script sketch (knowledge/aria/bin/nocturne-digest.sh)\n1. cd $PERS && git fetch sophon-bare (or file://) + compare HEAD vs\n   audit/iar/nocturne/LAST-DIGESTED-HEAD (state file).\n2. Same HEAD -> exit 0 (model never loads).\n3. Else: git diff --stat LAST..HEAD + the changed memory files\n   (journals, LOGS, relay open->answered, DECISIONS.org) -> compose\n   prompt -> iar.sh --one-shot --agent nocturne --model\n   deepseek-v4.1-flash:cloud --ctx 262144 --timeout 1800.\n4. On success: write LAST-DIGESTED-HEAD = new HEAD.\n5. Never touches DIGEST.md. Never exits nonzero (feeder pattern).\n\n* Timer sketch (sophon)\n/etc/systemd/system/nocturne-digest.service (oneshot, User=nacho,\nExecStart=/usr/local/bin/nocturne-digest.sh, TimeoutStartSec=2400)\n/etc/systemd/system/nocturne-digest.timer (OnCalendar=*-*-* 13:00\nUTC = 10:00 -03, Persistent=true, RandomizedDelaySec=300)\nEnable + start timer. First run watched live.\n\n* Open items (not blocking first run)\n- JSON-mode quirk: if the wrapper needs structured output, ask for\n  fenced JSON in prose i