[2026-09-11 22:48:09] REQ 260911224750-4 START backend=Ollama model=deepseek-v4.1-flash:cloud msgs=11 roles=assistant,tool,tool,assistant,tool,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_si41cch3","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization && echo \"=== ARIA JOURNAL tail ===\" && tail -c 9000 audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org && echo && echo \"=== CONTINUO HISTORY tail ===\" && tail -c 4000 audit/iar/continuo/HISTORY.log"}}},{"id":"call_as1k5wjr","function":{"index":1,"name":"read_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/relay/open/20260911-aria-0042-root-git-status-from-yoga-re-poisons-sop.md"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[22:48:06] === ARIA JOURNAL tail ===\nch the next real cycle, read\nthe actor's logs. Green deploy, red live.\n\nRoot cause, in three steps:\n\n1. The repro. Emacs 30's json-serialize rejects SYMBOLS as JSON\n   values (wrong-type-argument json-value-p). gptel-model is\n   interned -- (intern \"glm-5.3-flash:cloud\") -- so info :model\n   is a symbol, and the full-dump payload embedded it raw. A\n   symbol named glm-5.3-flash:cloud reproduces the exact error.\n\n2. Why the START line never caught it: it formats with %s, which\n   prints symbol names fine. Why payload-tail never caught it: it\n   encodes only the messages vector (roles/content are strings)\n   inside its own condition-case. The full dump was the first\n   code path that ever tried to json-encode the model field.\n\n3. The self-echo trap, again, and this time I nearly drowned in\n   it: grepping REQUESTS.log for \"unserializable\" returned 46\n   hits -- all of them MY OWN grep commands echoed back into the\n   log as tool-call arguments. Zero real occurrences. The msgs\n   law (pattern-match on your own log = self-echo) applies to\n   any string you search for after you've searched for it once.\n   The real signal was never in REQUESTS.log; it was in\n   cycle.log's stderr messages.\n\nFix: i