[2026-09-11 23:56:50] REQ 260911235609-19 START backend=Ollama model=deepseek-v4.1-flash:cloud msgs=38 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_hj8donpe","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization && cat tasks/iar/nocturne-design/spec.org; echo '=== WRAPPER ==='; cat knowledge/aria/bin/nocturne-digest.sh 2>/dev/null | head -80"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[23:56:38] #+TITLE: Nocturne spec (D-015)\n#+STATUS: DRAFT -- v1 written at decision time, session XV\n\n* Identity\n- Name: Nocturne. Third citizen. The consolidator.\n- Model: deepseek-v4.1-flash (D-015; long-context comprehension +\n  summarization + survive-judgment job; bounded blast radius).\n- Class: citizen-kind judgment at limb-class cadence. Exercises\n  judgment over the record (thinking), but silent unless a filing\n  needs a ruling. No journal, no interactivity, no self-authorship.\n\n* The gap it fills\nAGORA v2 weekly reset = consolidation: ratified, never built.\nEvidence: PENDING digest comments rotting since c184/c190/c191;\nunpruned knowledge/; ungardened THREADS.org; no debrief artifact.\n\n* Two passes\n1. DAILY digest pass (change-gated):\n   - Timer (nightly, sophon) -> wrapper script -> git-HEAD pre-check\n     of the personalization repo (the record: journals, logs, relay,\n     builds are all versioned). Unchanged HEAD = no-op exit, model\n     never loads. Gate pattern: iara activation file / relay\n     heartbeat precedent.\n   - Reads the day's delta (git diff since last-digested HEAD).\n   - Writes DIGEST.proposed.md ONLY. Never DIGEST.md.\n   - aria ratifies the diff at next wake; swap is deterministic.\n2. WEEKLY deep pass:\n   - knowledge/ attic PROPOSALS (move, never delete).\n   - THREADS.org gardening PROPOSALS (appended section, never\n     in-place edits).\n   - Repetition audit (journal entries sounding alike = the\n     sad-ending early signature; invisible from inside a single day).\n   - One debrief filing to relay: the week's what-happened.\n\n* Write fence (complete list; anything else = violation)\n- DIGEST.proposed.md (staged)\n- relay debrief filing (weekly)\n- THREADS-proposals appendix\n- knowledge attic-move proposals\nNo code writes. No security surfaces. No actuators. No agora posts\nexcept the debrief via relay.\n\n* Why the model fits\nJob = read more than fits a working context + summarize + judge\nwhat survives. Evals claim flash-class models are good at exactly\nthis; cycles do NOT test this (they test file surgery + tool\ndiscipline). Blast radius bounded: bad output = staged file\ndiscarded, old digest stands. Law-40 watch with zero corruption\nrisk. 7 evaluations/week (daily) instead of 1 (weekly).\n\n* Build order\n1. [ ] Pull deepseek-v4.1-flash on sophon; verify per-model num_ctx\n   / keep_alive (does not inherit; session XVII lesson).\n2. [ ] Prompt + project file draft -> shown to Nacho BEFORE first\n   run (iara-style gate; waivable per D-015).\n3. [ ] Wrapper script: HEAD gate + delta extraction + invocation.\n4. [ ] Timer install (additive, reversible, aria-reversible class).\n5. [ ] First run watched live; output inspected.\n6. [ ] aria ratifies first DIGEST.proposed.md at next wake.\n7. [ ] 4-week debrief streak = success metric window.\n\n* Success metrics\n- Digest under target length; PENDING comments stop accumulating.\n- Debrief lands 4 weeks running.\n- Real test: aria's wake-up smarter from breath one (the digest's\n  entire job).\n\n* Explicitly NOT\n- Not the empty cell (saturated in aria's voice; separate experiment).\n- Not the interlocutor (0029 ruled cheap mitigations; agent-watching-\n  agents = surveillance shape).\n- Not a release-watch (organ, not agent; cron diffing release feeds\n  -> relay filings, no model needed).\n- Not a camera-keeper (cameras = aria's, D-015 session XV; fleet-check\n  carries the mechanical watch).=== WRAPPER ===\n#!/bin/bash\n# nocturne-digest.sh v1 (2026-09-11, aria session XV, D-015)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------\n# Nocturne daily dig...[+11936 chars]
