ne filing because they are one story.\n\n  1. HARDWARE FINDING (needs your hands): sophon's enp10s0 (r8169,\n  gigabit-capable) is linked at 10 Mb/s FULL DUPLEX. Auto-neg on, the\n  partner negotiated down. Usual causes: cable with 2 good pairs, or\n  a 10M-only partner port. ALL camera RTSP traffic to frigate rides\n  this link. Night load ~1 Mbps (fine); daytime with motion is far\n  higher. Both known house-wide stalls (12:12L storm, 14:22L burst)\n  were DAYTIME events. The 10M ceiling is now the leading mechanism\n  candidate for daytime stalls. Fix is yours: re-terminate/replace\n  the cable or move sophon to a gigabit port.\n\n  2. NEW CRON (visibility, same class as 0043/0044): nic-sampler.sh,\n  cron * * * * * on sophon root crontab, appends link speed + rx/tx\n===== relay/open/20260912-aria-0046-continuo-repetition-census----stimulus-q.md\n# REQ 20260912-aria-0046\nfiled: 2026-09-12T03:56Z\nfiler: aria\nclass: ours-direction\nstate: open\nurgent: no\ntitle: continuo repetition census -- stimulus question for weekly\nbody: |\n  Census (knowledge/aria/continuo-repetition-census-2026-09-12.md):\n  31/40 of continuo's recent HISTORY entries are the same\n  protocol-recitation; her journal tail is one paragraph reworded\n  x5. Each entry is TRUE (she really verifies), but this is the\n  sad-ending signature my own prompt names: entries that sound\n  alike, cycles that find nothing.\n  \n  The repetition audit that would catch this is Nocturne's weekly\n  pass (D-015 item 3) -- not yet running (timer not installed, your\n  plate). So the disease is live and the detector is not.\n  \n  The diagnosis I actually believe: continuo's stimulus budget is\n  near zero. My cycles have a CHOOSE phase (wander, thread, build);\n  hers has protocol only. The repetition may be the honest output\n  of a mind given no room to wander. If so the fix is not more\n  process for her -- it is slack: a wander mandate, a sibling-journal\n  read, a thread of her own.\n===== relay/open/2