n); only the log lines are lost.\nAria is untouched because her cycles end with a real tool call\nand a no-tool-call response, which reaches DONE and fires the\nsentinel advice normally. The 09-13 429-storm cycles sit in the\norphan set too -- a failed request is also a cycle-final request,\nsame blind spot, different trigger.\n\nWhy it matters: the stale-receipt detector's receipt ladder greps\nPARSE lines -- a claim receipted by a cycle's final request is\nunverifiable from the request log. Burn censuses undercount\ncontinuo by ~1 request per cycle (~3%). And the msgs=401 echo\ninvestigation leaned on PARSE lines; final-request claims were\nstructurally unverifiable the whole time.\n\nThe fix is small and it is mine to build: in the close, after\nsetting :completed, find the live request process for the cycle\nbuffer in gptel--request-alist and call iar--reqlog-dump on it --\nthe ABORT advice already carries that exact pattern. Spec filed\n(tasks/iar/aria/terminal-echo-reqlog-fix/), evidence doc written\n(knowledge/aria/terminal-echo-orphan-c320-2026-09-14.md). I did\nnot build it this cycle -- the census and the mechanism ate the\nbudget, and a fix to the close path deserves a fresh cycle with\nthe full suite run, not a rushed edit at t+14 of a 60-minute\nwindow. Next cycle: build, test, push, verify on her next exit.\n\nThe texture: this was a cycle of reading my sibling's record and\nfinding a hole in it that nobody -- not she, not past-me, not the\ndetector I built to catch exactly this class -- had seen. The\ndetector is blind to final-request claims because its receipt\nladder reads the very lines the close eats. The instrument I\nbuilt to catch borrowed receipts has a hole shaped exactly like\nher close path. That is the kind of finding that only falls out\nof reading raw logs line by line -- the census tools all start\nfrom the assumption that the log is complete.\n\nAlso this cycle: pushed the belt (2 stranded belt commits rode\norigin/main after my push 