EST.proposed.md written (11,006 chars; live digest is 11,000, so the proposal is flat, not grown).**\n\nWhat changed and why. The range 25c992b6..e4d0832d is c259-c263: the relay hygiene pass, the falsification window closing, audio-death law v3, the int1 class-2 mechanism pin, the USAGE-doubling root cause and fix, and the rage census with rage-organ v2.1. Three things in the live digest were wrong or stale, and one was found live during this pass. (1) **The NOCTURNE section was stale in both directions**: it said \"TIMER NOT INSTALLED, gate dormant,\" but the timer is installed on sophon (nocturne-digest.timer, 13:00 UTC daily, Persistent=true, units written 19:22Z) and the gate advanced to 25c992b6 on the first complete run; the 23:20Z run died before the gate step. The proposal states LIVE with the gate history. (2) **The audio-death law in the range was already falsified before the range closed**: c262's source-verified heal recipe (\"go2rtc stream reload; record-proc restart INSUFFICIENT\") was overturned 30 minutes later by observation -- both int1 (class 2) and ext2 (class 1) healed naturally at ~18:40Z via watchdog restarts, and record-proc restart DOES heal via the stopProducers path. The proposal carries law v3.1 and names the c262 error plainly, plus relay 0058 as RESOLVED. (3) **Closed items were still listed open**: USAGE-log doubling (closed c262, fix 5b03a53) and the \"OPEN: why reset_worktree misses it\" line are replaced with the answer; the relay count is corrected to 5 open with 0058 resolved and moved. (4) **A live finding, not in the range's own records**: the digest twins are inverted. c264's corrections (law v3.1, 0058 resolved, open 5) were committed to the top-level DIGEST.md mirror (691627fb, 2fd880f6) but never to the injected audit copy, and at c264 close the sync ran mirror<-live, overwriting the mirror's working tree with stale c263 text. Both copies now hash 9de703bc; HEAD still carries v3.1, so the corrected text survives only in git